// SR 942.20 — Section 8 Duty to Provide Information, Cooperation and Confidentiality
// generated by src/parse.py. Do not edit by hand.

:NOTE
English is not an official language of the Swiss Confederation. This translation is provided for information purposes only and has no legal force.

:INFO
Art. 17 Duty to provide information
Parties to agreements affecting competition, undertakings with market power and third parties involved in the market must provide the Price Supervisor with all the information required and make the necessary documents available. Third parties are not obliged to disclose manufacturing or business secrets.
|

:NOTE
Amended by Annex No 3 of the Cartel Act of 6 Oct. 1995, in force since 1 July 1996 (AS 1996 546, 1805; BBl 1995 I 468).
|

:INFO
Art. 18 Cooperation
The Price Supervisor may request federal, cantonal and communal offices and supervisory authorities as well as business organisations to cooperate in his or her investigations and to provide the necessary documents.
|

:INFO
Art. 19 Official and business secrets
1 The Price Supervisor shall maintain official secrecy.
2 He or she may not disclose any business secrets.

